Session: 2026-10-15 14:52 UTC
Plan: plan/2026/09/19-phase-18-compatibility-release-gate.md
Scope: P18-V01 Remoting Bootstrap socket-buffer, watermark, and allocator timing

Source review
- Pinned Java direct Bootstrap reads socket buffers, custom write watermarks,
  and allocator choice while `start()` constructs the Bootstrap.
- `createBootstrap()` for a matched proxy CIDR reads socket buffers when that
  CIDR is first used and caches the Bootstrap; it does not set custom write
  watermarks or the allocator option. Rust previously used construction-time
  snapshots for all routes.

Implementation
- Code commit: 7b00a52f fix(remoting): sample bootstrap settings at source timing.
- Added live Rust adapters for socket send/receive buffers, write watermarks,
  and frame-pool enablement. Direct settings are captured at `start()`; proxy
  socket buffers are captured and cached per CIDR. Proxy channels use default
  watermarks and do not use the optional frame pool.
- Added Rust regressions for direct start snapshots, per-CIDR proxy caching,
  direct watermark validation, and retryable startup after invalid settings.
  Extended Java `RemotingLiveConfigProbe` to inspect direct and proxy Bootstrap
  option maps, including reuse and later-CIDR reads.
- A first all-feature Rust run failed because an existing frame-limit child
  test invoked the internal connection helper without calling `start()`. The
  helper now follows the public lifecycle and shuts down its client. The full
  Remoting suite then passed; the targeted frame-limit test passed again after
  the cleanup adjustment.
- Updated the five setting rows and appended release evidence.
  No plan files were edited.

Verification
- `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-remoting --all-features --locked`: passed;
  91 unit, 6 codec, 1 fuzz regression, 5 security, 95 transport, 5 doctests.
- Targeted `java_frame_max_length_property_is_applied_to_new_connections`:
  passed after the test lifecycle correction.
- `cargo clippy -p rocketmq-classic-remoting --all-targets --all-features
  --locked -- -D warnings`: passed.
- `cargo fmt --all -- --check`: passed.
- `mvn -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml verify`: passed; 37 scenarios,
  Remoting live-config probe, Java/Rust cross-decodes and fixture checks.
- `git diff --check`: passed before code commit.

Status
- The direct/proxy source-timing rows for socket buffers, write watermarks,
  and allocator selection are closed on 7b00a52f.
- Other Remoting settings, full bidirectional P18-V01 reconciliation,
  final-revision workspace P18-V02, current-revision GitHub Ubuntu/P18-V04,
  Phase 19 local Docker/Broker automation, and release version/registry checks
  remain open. Owner-run deployment/live Broker checks remain manual.

Session: 2026-10-15 15:00 UTC
Plan: plan/2026/09/19-phase-18-compatibility-release-gate.md
Scope: P18-V01 Remoting `useTLS` setting timing

Source review
- Java builds its SSL context when the client is constructed, then reads
  mutable `useTLS` for each new channel. If no SSL context was captured,
  enabling the flag later cannot add TLS to the channel.
- Rust previously used `TransportMode` as both context and channel decision,
  so it could not turn TLS off for a later channel after construction.

Implementation
- Code commit: 04c219dc fix(remoting): read TLS toggle for new channels.
- Rust now exposes a live `useTLS` adapter, captures the connector at
  construction, and samples the toggle per new connection before handshake.
  Existing connections retain their established transport mode.
- Added Rust loopback coverage for post-start disable/enable and for enabling
  the toggle when no TLS connector was captured. Extended Java
  `RemotingLiveConfigProbe` to mutate `useTLS` after client start and verify a
  new channel omits `SslHandler`.
- Updated the Remoting inventory and release checklist. No plan files were
  edited.

Verification
- `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-remoting --all-features --locked`: passed;
  91 unit, 6 codec, 1 fuzz regression, 5 security, 97 transport, 5 doctests.
- `cargo clippy -p rocketmq-classic-remoting --all-targets --all-features
  --locked -- -D warnings`: passed.
- `cargo fmt --all -- --check`: passed.
- `mvn -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml verify`: passed; 37 scenarios,
  Remoting live-config probe, Java/Rust cross-decodes and fixture checks.
- `git diff --check`: passed before code commit.

Status
- The Remoting `useTLS` setting-timing row is closed on 04c219dc.
- Broad P18-V01, final-revision full-workspace P18-V02, current-revision GitHub
  Ubuntu/P18-V04 evidence, Phase 19 local Docker/Broker automation, and release
